Z||000003||Raydar||10-23-2001||05:42 PM||||The injectors can make a noise that sounds like improper valve adjustment. Most noticeable at idle, though. <BR>I'm guessing an exhaust manifold leak, too. <BR>You can take about 4-5 feet of garden hose and use it like a stethescope to listen for noises. Leave the metal end on it, or else it'll melt if you touch your manifold. <BR>Glad you've got it running!<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
